fact WorkItem(id: "WI-727", description: some(value: "Variadic argument capture (proposal 056, docs/proposals/056-variadic-argument-capture.md): collect the named arguments NOT matched to a declared parameter into a single named-tuple (record) value, so an operation or rule whose arguments are a VARIADIC set of names (not a fixed parameter list) resolves through the ordinary path with NO op-identity-keyed typer code. TWO FACES of one capability: (1) OPERATION parameter -- a trailing capture param whose type is an open/row record (the record analog of an open effect row, 045); ordinary DotApply arg-matching, after binding declared params, collects the leftover named args into it as a named tuple typed field-by-field from the call, reaching the runtime as an ordinary Value::Tuple (no compile-time spec-splicing). (2) RULE-HEAD rest-pattern -- rule f(?r, ?rest..) <=> ... binds the leftover args as a record OCCURRENCE a [simp] macro (043.1) reads (the variadic analog of join's fixed (?r1,?r2,?cond) head). PLUS the Without[T, Drop] type constructor (dual of 052 join's Concat, WI-726): reduces at the return-type normalization boundary, dropping from named-tuple T every field named in record Drop; the membership + constant-type checks (a Drop field naming no T field, a mismatched type) are LOAD errors there, so the capture itself stays unconstrained/generic. DRIVING CLIENT: WI-714 fix -- r.fix(x: 1, z: 2) restricts relation columns to constants and drops them; the keys x/z are DYNAMIC columns of the receiver relation, not declared params, so there is nothing for ordinary arg-matching to bind them against. Without 056, fix needs an op_sym==Relation.fix typer recognizer -- the per-op recognizer the join->Concat 'no op-name-keyed typer code' discipline forbids; with 056, fix is an ordinary operation (capture param + Without in the return type + one host builtin that reads the record and wraps guarded + drops columns), nothing in the typer keyed on fix. AFFECTS: grammar (capture marker on a param / a rule-head rest-pattern), loader+typer (arg-match collects the residue into a named tuple; the Without reduction), docs/kernel-language.md (par.4 parameters, par.8.3 rule heads); runtime: none new (an ordinary named-tuple value). OPEN QUESTIONS: marker spelling (open-record (..) vs a row var (x:T,..R) vs a keyword); named-only vs positional variadic (fix needs NAMED; positional has no client yet -- design symmetric, defer); at most one capture param, trailing. ACCEPTANCE: an operation with a capture parameter resolves a call carrying extra named args, binding them as a named tuple typed from the call; the Without type constructor reduces a relation schema (drop + 1-collapse/Unit, load error on a missing field); WI-714 fix reimplemented as an ordinary op with no op-identity-keyed typer code; cargo-test green via rustland/scripts/test.sh. Rust-only (grammar/loader/typer; scaland has no typer). Draft proposal 056 written this session from the WI-714 fix design thread."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-17T05:00:42Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-727", author: "user", content: "SETTLED SURFACE (converged with user over a Socratic thread; supersedes the OQ #1 open-marker framing in the description): operation fix[R](p: Relation, ...args: R) -> Relation[T = Without[T = p.T, Drop = R]]. [R] = an ORDINARY explicit type parameter (042), INFERRED from the captured args exactly as join[L,R] infers from its operands (NOT a new row-var syntax). ...args = the ONE new grammar token, the rest/capture marker. R = the captured record's type, a first-class handle the return type consumes via Without[Drop=R]. NO inline open-record type (?R); NO effect-set {} for args. KEY: effects FLATTEN ({X,Y}=set union) but argument records DON'T (named+structured) -> capture rides record () not set {}, and schema combine/drop is an EXPLICIT name-aware type constructor (Concat/Without), never {}-algebra; join's own signature already splits E={r1.E,r2.E} (flatten) vs T=Concat[A,B] (explicit). Prior art: Without=TS Omit<T,K> (project=Pick), ...args capture=TS object-rest {...rest}; Scala 3 named tuples have subset pattern match but NO rest-capture / NO open rows -> the internal 045 row precedent carries this. fix[R] dodges WI-726 (R types the args capture, not Relation.T). Proposal 056 §2-3 updated to this. RESOLVED OQs: #1 marker=...args:R + [R]; #2 positional leftovers unify into R as _N (one mechanism covers named+positional).", at: "2026-07-16T19:07:57Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-727", author: "user", content: "GRAMMAR PROBED conflict-free (empirical, this session, tree-sitter 0.25.10): the ...args capture marker is a single FUSED lexer token, added as optional(field('rest', token('...'))) on the param rule -- the exact technique the distribute-dot .( uses (token(seq('.','('))) to diverge at the LEXER from . / .( / A.B and avoid GLR/precedence fights. Results: tree-sitter generate = clean/no conflicts; parsing fix[R](p: Relation, ...args: R) attaches the rest marker to exactly the ...args param (p: Relation untouched), NO ERROR/MISSING; x.field + rel.(name,age) + Ns.Sort.member coexist; FULL 176-test corpus passes. So the grammar side is a one-line param-rule change, already validated -- no design/tokenization risk remains for the ... marker.", at: "2026-07-16T20:18:09Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-727", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED on branch wi-727-variadic-capture (94dbe449 impl + 3594585a review fixes). Full workspace green 2915/0; 11 wi727_fix tests + grammar corpus (177/177). Pieces: (1) grammar ...args fused-token marker on param; (2) parse Param.rest + loader at-most-one/trailing validation + KB side-table op_capture_params (gated on conformance); (3) typer normalize_variadic_capture folds leftover named args into ONE named-tuple record (Expr::Constructor{TupleLiteral}) bound to the capture param, single-pass at the top of check_apply_iter Path 1 — all downstream matching (R inference, coverage, node reorder) runs UNCHANGED; (4) Without[T,Drop] type ctor = dual of Concat, membership+type checks live in the reduction (they give the unconstrained capture its meaning), residual 1-collapses; (5) fix[R](p: Relation, ...args: R) -> Relation[T=Without[T=p.T,Drop=R], E=p.E] + host builtin (guarded eq + column drop, bag semantics). NO op-identity-keyed typer code (code-review altitude agent explicitly PASSED this). /code-review high (4 agents): 1 real finding (capture recorded even when validation failed -> gated) + conventions (silent Err drop -> explicit; None==None Unit test -> zip-guarded) + dedup refactor (reduce_concat/reduce_without -> shared reduce_binary_type_ctor + BinaryTypeCtor config; type_mentions_sort + one combined gate walk; collapse_schema; eval find_column). DEFERRED (proposal 056 s5, no client): positional-leftover capture; the rule-head rest-pattern face (s2.3, optional for fix); polymorphic-column type-check in Without is best-effort. KNOWN EDGE (loud error, not silent): a relation column literally named like the capture param (args) hits the idempotency guard -> Without 'drop operand must be a record' error.", at: "2026-07-17T05:00:40Z")
